  "rhythmSettingsTitle": "Rhythm",
  "rhythmExplainer": "After a check, every nest gets a new date. If something was in it — an egg, a chick, a bird sitting on it — the base interval applies. If it was empty, several times running, the gap is stretched: the ladder below says by how much. As soon as something is found again it drops back to the base interval in ONE step. The ladder climbs slowly and falls at once, because the two errors cost different amounts: checking a dead nest too often wastes an hour, checking a live one too rarely loses a clutch.",
  "rhythmReadOnlyHint": "Only the coordination can change these numbers. Everybody can see them — a date you are told to trust without seeing where it came from is a date people override.",
  "rhythmDaysSuffix": "days",
  "rhythmBaseLabel": "Base interval",
  "rhythmBaseHelp": "How long until the next check when there was something in the nest.",
  "rhythmLadderLabel": "Ladder for empty nests",
  "rhythmLadderHelp": "The gaps when a nest has been empty several times running. The last step is the cap — it is reached and not exceeded, because anything with a roof over it can be occupied again.",
